<!--
NODrugInhaler.DES - Defines inhalation delivery of NO in HumMod

Overview
This file models of Nitric Oxide (NO) when administered via inhalation.
It manages dosing, lung retention, and systemic circulation absorption.

1. Dosing Variables: Tracks inhaled dose, last dose time, and cumulative doses.
2. Respiratory Timing: Computes inhalation time using the respiratory rate.
3. Lung vs. Systemic Distribution: Splits the dose into lung-retained and systemically absorbed fractions.
4. Drug Clearance

 How to Replicate for Another Drug
1. Change `<name> NODrugInhaler </name>` to `<name> NewDrugInhaler </name>`.
2. Modify Dose values to reflect the new drug's inhaled concentration (e.g., ppm for gases).
3. Adjust LungFraction based on how much of the drug stays in the lungs vs. systemic circulation.
4. Modify the clearance rate (K) to match the new drug’s elimination properties.

-->

HumMod / NODrug

Created : 15-Jul-13
Revised : 
Author : W Pruett
Copyright : 2013-2013
By : University Of Mississippi Medical Center

<structure><name> NODrugInhaler </name> <!-- Defines the inhaler-based NO administration -->

<variables>

<parm><name> Dose </name><val> 20 </val></parm> <!-- Defines dose in ppm -->
<var><name> TimeLastDose </name><val> UNDEFINED </val></var> <!-- Tracks last dose timestamp, initially undefined -->
<var><name> TotalDoses </name><val> 0.0 </val></var> <!-- Counts total doses administered, initially 0 -->
<var><name> CumulativeDose </name><val> 0.0 </val></var> <!-- Accumulates total dose intake, initially 0 -->
<var><name> TimeSpan </name></var> <!-- Inhalation duration per breath -->
<var><name> K </name><val> 0 </val></var> <!-- Drug clearance rate -->
<parm><name> LungFraction </name><val> 0.4 </val></parm> <!-- Fraction of dose retained in the lungs -->

</variables>

<equations>

<diffeq>
  <name> Mass </name> <!-- Tracks current drug amount in the system -->
  <integralname> Mass </integralname>
  <initialval> 0.0 </initialval> <!-- Starts with no inhaled NO present -->
  <dervname> Change </dervname>
  <errorlim> 0.01 </errorlim> <!-- Error tolerance for integration. It is probably that the faster the system, the "lower" the error tolerance should be. -->
</diffeq>

</equations>

<definitions>
  
<block><name> Inhale </name> <!-- Defines inhalation dynamics -->

<def>
  <name> TimeSpan </name> <!-- Calculates inhalation duration per breath -->
  <val> 60 / RespiratoryCenter-Output.Rate </val>
</def>

<def>
  <name> K </name> <!-- Computes drug clearance rate -->
  <val> 2 / TimeSpan </val> <!-- higher breathing rates lead to shorter TimeSpan values, and therefore higher clearance rates (K) ... in NO, suggests clearance twice per breathing cycle. -->
</def>

<def>
  <name> Mass </name>
  <val> Mass + Dose </val> <!-- adds new inhaled dose to NO -->
</def>
<def>
  <name> TimeLastDose </name>
  <val> System.X </val> <!-- system time = time last dose -->
</def>

<def>
  <name> TotalDoses </name>
  <val> TotalDoses + 1.0 </val> <!-- total number of inhalations -->
</def>

<def>
  <name> CumulativeDose </name>
  <val> CumulativeDose + Dose </val> <!-- total number of NO inhaled -->
</def>

</block>

<block>
<name> Dervs </name> <!-- Defines drug elimination and lung distribution -->

<def>
  <name> Change </name>
  <val> - K * Mass </val> <!-- drug clearance with negative K (clearance rate) value -->
</def>

<def>
  <name> NODrugSL.Mass </name>
  <val> NODrugSL.Mass - ( ( 1 - LungFraction ) * Change ) </val>
</def> <!-- Fraction of drug entering systemic circulation -->

<def>
  <name> NODrugLung.Mass </name>
  <val> NODrugLung.Mass - ( LungFraction * Change ) </val>
</def> <!-- Fraction retained in lungs -->

</block>

<block><name> Reset </name> <!-- Allows resetting dose tracking -->

<def>
  <name> TimeLastDose </name>
  <val> UNDEFINED </val>
</def>

<def>
  <name> TotalDoses </name>
  <val> 0.0 </val>
</def>

<def>
  <name> CumulativeDose </name>
  <val> 0.0 </val>
</def>

</block>

</definitions>
</structure>

End
